                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The Ghibli-inspired art is so gorgeous that I bought a cheap bundle just to get a look at Transcend. It really is stunning (except maybe your character, who looks like Bobby Hill).\n\nKeeping the nature of Early Access in mind, there's not much of a game here yet. I made it through the four currently available chapters in 34 minutes, and they played like a needlessly drawn-out tutorial. I mean, that's pretty much all they were. Here's how to play... and, it's over. Calling them separate chapters is probably disingenuous.\n\nThere's a fair amount of textual dialog and a few superficial reply options. The story, such as it is, isn't compelling. If Transcend is to be successful, the text really needs to get out of the way of the real star of the show - the art, and the supreme potential it has to create an amazing world. \n\nI found the combat awkward and punishing. There are some nice things about it, like the weighty clank of swords colliding, but for the most part it feels unpolished. I'm not big into hack and slash, so maybe it just wasn't for me, but I'm guessing it just plain needs a lot of improvement. Nailing the right flow is critical. \n\nHonestly, if I had my way, the dev would ditch the combat style altogether and repurpose the world and his/her talent for something that emphasizes exploration. With all the mechanics focused on gladiatorial combat, the rest just feels like window dressing and wasted potential. I'm adamant that the look of the game could contribute greatly to a truly affecting experience, but it's just not there - the theme doesn't realy come through. Not with the story and mechanics at present. \n\nEven with seven more chapters, if they're like the fisrt four, I wouldn't recommend Transcend. If the next seven are better realized and more fleshed out, I could see some people digging the combat in a more polished form. And I would play it just to walk through it, if that were possible, because my god does it look pretty.",
